schema: test/v2
level: working-unit
epic: E-REDESIGN
wu: E-REDESIGN.W3
tests:
  unit:
    waived: "The WU adds no product code — its whole output is one design run under docs/work/, and git diff --stat epic/redesign HEAD -- ui/src/ is empty. This is the E-DFLOW.W9 precedent the epic plan cites for exactly this case: the WU 'touches no product code or screens'. There is nothing to unit-test; the screen's own unit tests are W4's, where FlowList.test.tsx lands — today the only screen in ui/src/ with no adjacent test file — and each will assert the states and absences THIS design declares."
  integration:
    waived: "Same precedent. There is no bounded contract in code to exercise: the contract IS the run doc, and cargo xtask verify-doc is what judges its shape. The eleven Tier-1 items, the receipt's slug coverage against the rulebook on disk, and the mockup's mount rule are the mechanical checks that stand in for an integration test here, and all are green."
  e2e:
    waived: "Same precedent. No user-visible surface moves — the diff is two HTML files. UC-4's e2e runs against the rebuilt screen in W4 and the epic's own at W11. NOT waived on the grounds that nothing could move: W2's e2e waiver was voided by a review finding that its components were unreachable from the bundle, so the question was asked again here and answered by the empty ui/src/ diff rather than by assumption."
verified:
  - "cargo xtask verify-doc docs/work/2026-09-04-flow-list-shell.html — green (design-run). receipt 17/17 soft · 14 satisfied · 2 n/a · 1 violated; hard rules 13/13 machine-checked; design-allow 0 live suppressions."
  - "cargo xtask verify-doc docs/work/2026-09-04-redesign-w3-plan.html — green (wu-plan). Four wu-plan items present and non-empty; every relative link resolves."
  - "cargo xtask ui specimens --check — ok, 5 mounts, 2 buttons, clean console over file://. The gate asserts what a reader cannot see: every mockup zone mount non-empty AND no thrown error, rejected promise or console.error. A design run that hand-draws a component or mounts a broken one fails here."
  - "Real-browser measurement of the mockup, not jsdom, in the same headless Chrome the render gate uses. Every status carries its tone AND its reason phrase from the registry StatusPill: 200 rgb(76,195,138) '200 OK' · 201 ok '201 Created' · 304 rgb(174,166,156) '304 Not Modified' · 403 rgb(229,72,77) '403 Forbidden' · 500 warn '500 Internal Server Error' · null muted 'pending'. This is the epic's third defect verified as fixed on the designed surface."
  - "The pending row measured: DurationText renders rgba(0,0,0,0) with aria-hidden and select-none — genuinely invisible while holding the column open, so an in-flight row does not shift when it resolves. The design's still-at-rest quality is a measured property here, not a claim."
  - "The truncation verdict measured: the path cell computes text-overflow:ellipsis with the full value on the row's title attribute, and only row 5 of six actually cuts — the cut happens where the value exceeds the cell, not everywhere. The mockup's detail pane sits at the real pane token (380px), which is the condition that produces it."
  - "Both mockup states rendered and read: populated (6 rows, count '6 flows') and empty (Notice with its detail line, count '0 flows'). The toggle crosses exactly the states the Interaction table names."
  - "git hash-object docs/design-rules/design-rules-index.html — aeff5b0fb4dea94ab5f0b7c385b8188786666e8a, compared against the receipt's pin at the close (step ①) and again after each review round. Unmoved, so receipt·rulebook-stale is silent and the receipt is a claim about the rulebook actually on disk."
  - "git diff --stat epic/redesign HEAD -- ui/src/ — empty. The design-WU boundary the epic plan sets ('Design WUs commit nothing under ui/src/') holds mechanically."
  - "node scripts/design-registry.mjs — 27 entries, read once at the start and frozen for the run. Every verdict in the Elements table is judged against the @use/@avoid text this emitted."
note: "THE RUN CARRIES A VIOLATED RECEIPT ROW ON PURPOSE, and that is the single most important thing to check at Tier-3. wrap-not-truncate and display-equals-payload are both recorded violated for the host and path cells. The argument is that four of the six row cells clear the rule BY CONSTRUCTION — every registry component with a known maximum width sets its own whitespace-nowrap, and the screen adds nothing — while a path is unbounded in a fixed-height virtualized row, where the three alternatives each break a Frame constraint. A reviewer should attack that: is the fixed row height genuinely a constraint or a preference, and does the title attribute plus the detail pane really pay the cost. THREE REVIEW ROUNDS ALREADY MOVED THIS RUN, and all are recorded in its review item rather than smoothed away. (1) The assembled mockup contradicted its own Layout sketch — the detail pane rendered below the list instead of beside it, and no row truncated, leaving the run's central argument undemonstrated. Fixed by adding the missing zone wrapper and setting the pane to its real width. (2) A reviewer asked for centred status numbers; three variants were rendered and compared in a browser before choosing, because centring the values alone leaves the STATUS label pinned right and the pair loses its shared edge — Tune T4 centres both. (3) A reviewer questioned free-text method/status filters, and this CORRECTED A FALSE PREMISE IN THE RUN: the Field row had argued all three keys substring-match server-side, but store.rs:54 shows only host does — method is eq_ignore_ascii_case and status an exact u16. The row now states exactness per key and blocked-on carries three options unpicked, because a status class query (4xx) is not expressible against the current API at all. A fourth comment ('no need the date') was a mockup artifact, not a design issue: a hardcoded fixture date aged overnight into TimestampText's S2 cross-day state. The fixture now derives from today; the prefix itself is the component's state and a screen may not suppress it. A SECOND REVIEW ROUND LANDED ON THIS TIP (5869a46). Six finders and eight verifiers ran over 7290e30; every blocker and important was refuted on inspection, and three nits were real and fixed: a stale Tune citation (T4 had been renumbered T5 by the previous round), a mermaid loader over a doc with no diagram, and a fixture calling new Date() per row where a midnight-straddling render could split the list across TimestampText S1 and S2. A fourth finding is not this run's: a verifier trying to refute the hard-rule claim found that wrap-not-truncate's Tier-1 predicate cannot see a mockup at all - the tokenizer treats a babel script block as opaque raw text, and the flow spec REQUIRES the mockup to mount from exactly such a block, so verify-doc reports 13/13 hard rules green over markup it never read. Verified both ways (the same element in static HTML reds immediately) and recorded on the run's blocked-on for the harness, because every design run shares the hole. WHAT NO CHECK HERE PROVES: that a verdict is TRUE. verify-doc proves the receipt is complete and well-formed, never that a satisfied was earned. That is Tier-3's job and it is why this note is not the gate."
